c Correct simple Tseitin transformation
c Original: (x1 ∨ x2) ∧ (¬x1 ∨ x3)
c With auxiliary y: y ↔ (x1 ∨ x2), and require y ∧ (¬x1 ∨ x3)
c y ↔ (x1 ∨ x2) expands to:
c  (¬y ∨ x1 ∨ x2)  - if y then at least one of x1,x2
c  (y ∨ ¬x1)        - if x1 then y
c  (y ∨ ¬x2)        - if x2 then y
c Final constraints: y ∧ (¬x1 ∨ x3) means:
c  y                  - y must be true
c  (¬x1 ∨ x3)        - either not x1 or x3
p cnf 4 6
-4 1 2 0
4 -1 0
4 -2 0
4 0
-1 3 0
